From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kern0x1b <kern0x1b@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 16 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] WebGL through an ANGLE backend on EAGL

Upstream's only GL backend on Apple platforms is ANGLE's Metal renderer, which
needs an A7. This adds an ANGLE GLES backend on EAGL, the OpenGL ES 2.0 API this
hardware has: EAGL displays, pbuffer and IOSurface surfaces, IOSurface client
buffers through CVOpenGLESTextureCache, and the texture handover that puts a
canvas the GPU drew on the screen without a copy per frame. WebCore's GL context
points at it, WebGL runs on drivers without a framebuffer blit, a context that
asked for no alpha channel is served, and the textures taken from the cache are
let go. WebGL is turned on.
---
